<title>CHINA: China chemical plant resumes production after fire.</title>
<headline>China chemical plant resumes production after fire.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Beijing Dongfang Chemical Plant has resumed production in some sections of the complex after output stopped because of an explosion and fire last month, a factory official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Resin and acroleic acid equipment in our plant have resumed operations now, but ethylene production is still halted,&quot; the official said but refused to give further details.</p>
<p>Plant officials have has said it would be out of production for at least one year after the huge explosion, which killed three people and injured 64 on June 27.</p>
<p>It produced 110,000 to 120,000 tonnes of ethylene last year, officials said.</p>
